  "description": "This course covers the fundamentals of penetration testing and vulnerability assessment, including network scanning with Nmap, vulnerability scanning with Nessus, and exploit development using Metasploit. Topics include TCP/IP protocol analysis, SQL injection techniques, cross-site scripting (XSS), and buffer overflow attacks. Students will study the Open Web Application Security Project (OWASP) Top Ten vulnerabilities, conduct penetration testing using Kali Linux, and implement secure coding practices with OWASP ZAP. The course also covers ethical hacking principles, legal frameworks, and the use of Wireshark for packet analysis. Students will learn to design and execute penetration tests, document findings, and recommend remediation strategies using standardized methodologies such as PTES and OSSTMM.",
